#: r2/templates/adminloginsettings.html:25
msgid "Members can link a Google, Facebook, GitHub or Discord account to theirs (preferences, security) and then sign in with it instead of their password. It only signs in to accounts that linked it: nothing is matched by email address. Someone signing in with one that isn't linked yet can link it to their account with their password, or, while sign-ups are open, make a new account for it. A member with two-factor sign-in still enters their code. Settings saved here override the ini file and apply immediately."
